You ascend to the status of Demigod...--More--

I did it! After 18 straight hours in the terminal room, from 2pm to
8am the next day, I beat the most recent version (pl9) of nethack 3.0,
with over 2 million points to show for it! (Actually I've heard of
some games going on for weeks, so 18 hours may seem like a short time,
but my goal was just to make it without getting my weary Samurai
killed, and I wanted to get this game done before I got too busy in
schoolwork to play this anymore.) Before pl9, my strategy was to do
massive polypiles until I had over a dozen wands of wishing and oodles
of magic lamps, so I could basically do whatever I wanted to when I
met the Wiz. But in this game I had to prepare in advance, conserve
what came my way, and in general be smart and careful. It *is* very
rewarding to it without wish abuse, and to get your weapons from the
gods, etc. Anyway, details about this game follow:
(*** possible spoilers, of course ***)

I played Samurai, which I consider a good character in that he has
lots of St, Dx, and Co, and has good kicking ability for those killer
bees and locked chests. He's also a lawful character, so I can make
holy water and offerings (and get good weapons) at the same altar.

I have found the most important thing to do is wait until your
character starts out with a blindfold, then eat the first floating eye
you encounter. I consider the telepathy the most important intrinsic
in the game - just don't lose it as I did (in the stronghold level of
all places). I did have some good luck, such as a blessed potion of
invisibility found early on, as well as a couple of scrolls of
genocide (I first genocided rust monsters, followed by wiping out the
"T"roll and "L"ich classes.) Get a blessed unicorn horn as early as
possible (and eat the unicorn corpse) - very useful; also spend as
much time with nurses as you can, to get a good amount of hps.

I did do one mega-polypile, which was still useful although I couldn't
get extra wishes from it. (I piled up all the weapons, armor, and
protection rings from this huge army barracks, zapped a wand of
cancellation then polymorph at it, and proceeded to test out dozens of
new pieces of uncursed armor and rings.) I got my dragon scale mail
from a lamp which "had no oil", and my good weapons from my god (for
both Samurai and Mjollnir are Lawful.), but most everything else came
from the polypile.

When I teleported to level 50 in hell, I used my mirror to determine
when the Wiz was "right above my head", then level teleported to one
level above him and explored out all the other levels of hell (and
killed Vlad), so I would know where the < staircases are on my way up.
I killed the Wiz (first time) easily (Isn't there something you can do
with potions of paralysis here; i need to get him on a square other
than the one that the amulet is on, or else wait until he reincarnates
and then throw it at him?) But when he reincarnated, I suddenly found
myself in "Double trouble" (I don't remember *this* from earlier
versions), with two Wizard of Yendors and a Minotaur and a bunch of
other nasties beating the cr*p out of me - oops, took a few turns to
get my cursed gauntlets off and my ring of conflict on, which helped,
but I quickly died from these guys and used up a life saving amulet.

I'm concerned now; I won't last long at this rate, so I let them steal
the amulet and go up the stairs and build up my hps (and my score; I
notice that you are getting 3500+ points for each tough monster
killed.) I decide on my only chance to win this game - I go to the
level below the Wiz, kill a cockatrice and go up and and turn the
Wizard(s) to stone. I slowly went up level by level (keeping an eye on
how much food I had - easy to go from satiated to weak in just a few
^T's now), killing any cockatrice on each level and re-wielding it
(still have two amulets of live saving left in case I fall in a pit or
something). There were only a few times during which my corpse rotted
away, and anyway the Wiz can only take about 6 hits with Mjollnir
before expiring, so I was able to make it to the Endlevel and
finish what I consider to be my first "real" completion of Nethack...

